even as nevada continues to reopen  thousands of people across the state are  still out of a job that includes workers  on the las vegas strip  but a new bill at the state legislature  could help  orco mana joins us live on the strip  tonight to explain exactly how  orca well brian as more lights come back  on here on the las vegas strip  laid off hospitality workers are itching  to get back to work  the right to return bill would guarantee  them that chance  but not everyone thinks it's the best  path forward  we don't have jobs we don't have  anything for two decades norma flores  worked as a server at a local resort she  was laid off one year ago as covet 19  concerns shut down las vegas  now it's tough to make ends meet with a  pandemic  no more tips nothing and it's hard with  the unemployment  their take time to give it to me as  nevada reopens flores wants to get back  to work and she hopes senate bill 386  can help the right to return bill would  make casinos hotels and tourism related  industries offer laid off workers their  former jobs or similar positions  before considering other options but  some do not agree with the legislation  it's inappropriate republican state  senator keith pickard says  employees could falsely accuse resorts  of not offering them jobs  we're opening the door to litigation and  it makes it  very difficult for an employer to prove  they didn't do this  democratic senate majority leader nicole  cannizzaro who introduced the bill  acknowledges companies need protections  and she's working on that  for bad actors who want to take  advantage of that process we obviously  want to make sure there's some  enforcement mechanisms  some casino companies opposed the bill  saying it would result  in restrictive requirements but the  culinary union has a message for  employers  they have to realize the best thing for  this community to moving forward is give  it to the right person to go back  flores hopes everyone will get on board  we deserve  to come back to work  nevada lawmakers are working through the  details of the bill right now  next on the agenda is likely another  committee hearing  reporting live on the las vegas strip  tonight orco mana 8 news now
 

